#
# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify, which both read a file
# named `_headers` from the root of the published directory.
#
# The web build uses WebAssembly threads. Threads need SharedArrayBuffer, and
# browsers only expose SharedArrayBuffer to a cross-origin-isolated page — which
# means these two headers. Without them the page loads and then dies at startup
# on SharedArrayBuffer being undefined.
#
# These mirror what web/serve.py sends locally; if you change one, change both.
# GitHub Pages cannot set response headers at all, which is why it is not a
# deploy target for this build.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
